<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Package xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
    ONE CARD, THREE SECTIONS. 2026-08-25. The CONSTRUCTIVE half.

    STATUS: PREPARED, DRY-RUN VALIDATED, NOT DEPLOYED. The user deploys, not this
    repo.

    WHAT THIS PAYLOAD DOES
    ======================
    Collapses the three stacked BOV sidebar cards that shipped this morning into
    ONE card with three sections, per the user's design:

      section 1  Preferred Broker   the green hero panel (c/bovPreferredBroker),
                                    naming the broker CONTACT, firm demoted to a
                                    muted second line, "YES" pill removed
      section 2  Timeline           the merged NDA + Release Materials feed,
                                    unchanged
      section 3  BOV Responses      broker CONTACT + status, two columns

    THE FOUR MEMBERS BELOW, AND WHY EACH IS IN THE PAYLOAD
    =====================================================
    1. dispositionBuyerTimeline   the card itself. Gains a second wire
       (BovController.getSubmissions) that serves sections 1 and 3 from ONE
       payload, so the hero panel and the table can never name two different
       brokers.
    2. bovPreferredBroker         MOUNTED by section 1 rather than rebuilt. Gains
       `@api contactName`; loses the "YES" pill. It is SHARED with
       c/bovBrokerPanel at BOV Outreach, so the pill disappears there too, which
       the user asked for explicitly.
    3. bovBrokerPanel             CHANGED ONLY because of member 2: it passes the
       new `contact-name` attribute down and gains the getter behind it. Without
       it the BOV Outreach panel would render a firm where the record page
       renders a person.
    4. Disposition_Record_Page    loses the two itemInstances naming the deleted
       bundles.

    THE FLEXIPAGE AND THE DELETIONS MUST TRAVEL TOGETHER
    ====================================================
    A FlexiPage referencing a deleted LightningComponentBundle does not deploy.
    destructiveChangesPost.xml in this same directory removes the two bundles
    AFTER this payload lands, by which time the page no longer names them.
    POST, not PRE: the page edit has to be live first. Running either half alone
    fails or leaves a dangling reference.

    NOT IN THIS PAYLOAD, DELIBERATELY
    =================================
      * bovBrokerChangeHistory     untouched, still a standalone sidebar card.
        The user asked for it to stay exactly as it is.
      * Any Apex, object, field or permission set. NOTHING SERVER-SIDE CHANGED.
        The "only one row may show Selected" rule the user asked for is DISPLAY
        LOGIC inside the timeline bundle: the data model marks two rows Selected
        by design (the scored winner AND the preferred broker), and that design
        is correct elsewhere. The card derives what it shows and writes nothing.
      * The timeline's FlexiPage visibilityRule. Left byte for byte as it was, by
        instruction. It is narrower than the rule the two deleted cards carried,
        so sections 1 and 3 no longer appear before Release Materials; that
        consequence is recorded in the page's root comment and in the bundle's JS
        header rather than silently fixed.

    HOW TO RUN IT (only once authorised by the user)
    ===============================================
      sf project deploy start
        with the manifest flag                 pointing at this file
        with the post destructive changes flag pointing at destructiveChangesPost.xml
                                               in this same directory
        with the target org flag               set to usman&#45;dpeg
        with the dry run flag                  for a validation, dropped for the
                                               real deploy
    The flag prefixes are spelled out in words on purpose: an XML comment body
    cannot contain two consecutive hyphens.

    Rollback: every component here is recoverable from git history, and the two
    deleted bundles are recoverable from the commit that removes them.
    -->
    <types>
        <members>dispositionBuyerTimeline</members>
        <members>bovPreferredBroker</members>
        <members>bovBrokerPanel</members>
        <name>LightningComponentBundle</name>
    </types>
    <types>
        <members>Disposition_Record_Page</members>
        <name>FlexiPage</name>
    </types>
    <version>67.0</version>
</Package>
